Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?REQ-002=20=C2=A74=20logging=20+=202=20runtime?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20bug=20fixes=20found=20during=20phase-0=20bringup?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

LOGGING (REQ-002 §4):
- StoreStats: hint_ok + per-cause hint_drop_{openrouter_error,timeout,empty,
  parse_fail,other}, sandbox_fail (+by-exception), episodes_total/empty — all
  surfaced in as_metrics -> train.log + wandb every step.
- hint.py: per-cause classification via a ContextVar (build_error_hint keeps its
  pinned bare-string return; cause rides out-of-band, concurrency-safe).
- run.py: episode accounting + sandbox-failure classification in
  generate_trajectory, empty-transcript rejection, fail-loud sandbox-binary
  check when banking is in scope, eval-dump wiring.
- logger.py: evaluate/evaluate_pass1 guard per-task episode errors (a banking
  SandboxRuntimeError used to crash baseline mode) and append per-task eval
  JSONL rows.
- trainer.py: lr+tokens metrics, extended per-step log line, 3 sample
  teacher/student transcripts with per-token gap.

BUG FIXES (blocked all training on Baseten; found running phase-0 smoke):
- trainer.py setup_weight_sync: pin torch.cuda.set_device(self.device) before
  the vLLM weight-transfer rendezvous. It runs under asyncio.to_thread and
  CUDA's current device is per-thread, so the sender bound NCCL to GPU 0 and
  collided with the rollout worker ("Duplicate GPU detected: rank 0 and rank 1
  both on <bus>"). Affected every run, not just smoke.
- trainer.py build_dataloader: cfg.trainer.training_batch_size -> batch_size
  (the field is batch_size; the old name raised AttributeError at loop start).

